-- title:
--   Central transfer at scalars above a finite place
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, of prime degree $[L:K]$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$. Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, let $\varphi_v : \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ and $f_v : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ be locally constant with compact support, and assume $\varphi_v$ and $f_v$ satisfy the matching condition [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingOn`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L324) relative to the measures `semiLocalHaar K L v` and `localHaar K v`. Two conclusions are asserted. First, for every scalar matrix $\gamma = \mathrm{diag}(c,c)$ with $c \in K_v^\times$, every $\delta, y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with the image of $\gamma$ under base change equal to $y^{-1}\,\mathrm{normString}(\delta)\,y$, and every pair of Haar measures $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\{\gamma\}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ and $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{t : t\delta\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$ of $\delta$, coupled in the sense that the pushforward of $\tau'$ along $t \mapsto y^{-1}ty$ coincides with the pushforward of $\tau$ along base change: every twisted orbital integral $I'$ of $\varphi_v$ at $\delta$ with respect to $\tau'$ equals every orbital integral $I$ of $f_v$ at $\gamma$ with respect to $\tau$, where the latter means $I = \int f_v(x^{-1}\gamma x) w(x)\,d(\mathrm{localHaar})$ for some nonnegative measurable compactly supported $w$ with $\int_{Z(\gamma)} w(tx)\,d\tau = 1$ whenever $f_v(x^{-1}\gamma x) \neq 0$. Second, if a scalar $\gamma$ is the norm of no $\delta$, i.e. no $\delta$ and $y$ satisfy the above conjugacy relation, then for every Haar measure $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$, every orbital integral of $f_v$ at $\gamma$ with respect to $\tau$ is $0$.
--
--   This extends the local matching of $\varphi_v$ and $f_v$ from the regular semisimple elements, where it is imposed by hypothesis, to the central elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$: the twisted and untwisted orbital integrals agree at scalars that are norms, and the untwisted orbital integrals vanish at scalars that are not. It feeds the comparison of twisted and ordinary trace formulae used in the base change step for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over an extension of prime degree, and is invoked in the evaluation of $f_v$ at central elements and in the identification of twisted orbital integrals with multiples of $f_v$ at scalars.
